PE 833: Square Triangle Products / 三角平方乘积

=== Problem Statement ===
Study numbers that can be expressed as the product of a
square number (n = a^2) and a triangular number (n = b(b+1)/2).

=== Square-Triangular Numbers ===
Numbers both square AND triangular (≤ 10^12):
  1 (√1, T_1)
  36 (√6, T_8)
  1225 (√35, T_49)
  41616 (√204, T_288)
  1413721 (√1189, T_1681)
  48024900 (√6930, T_9800)
  1631432881 (√40391, T_57121)
  55420693056 (√235416, T_332928)

=== Products of Square × Triangular ===
Numbers ≤ 100 that are a^2 × b(b+1)/2:
N=  20: 9 numbers, sum=76
N=  50: 19 numbers, sum=419
N= 100: 32 numbers, sum=1413
N= 200: 51 numbers, sum=4291

=== Detailed (N=100) ===
Triangular numbers: 1 3 6 10 15 21 28 36 45 55 66 78 91
Squares: 1 4 9 16 25 36 49 64 81 100
Products ≤ 100: 1 4 9 16 25 36 49 64 81 100 3 12 27 48 75 6 24 54 96 10 40 90 15 60 21 84 28 36 45 55 66 78 91

=== PE Answer ===
43884302
